From 3c4e3b7b80488e161e599d739e2e3cb48cb01ae8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dylanoliverdo-coder
 <265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:55:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(post): incoming-stock review fixes: probes, torches,
 undercuts, the executing setup

Two independent reviews of this change found six cases; each is pinned by
a test in keep_law/incoming_stock_deficits that fails without its fix.

- A program of touch probes only plans nothing in the column sim (#108),
  so it was refused even with the acknowledgement. It is judged and noted
  the same way.
- A torch or wire removes material the column never sees (#670), and an
  undercut pass lowers no column top (#1444). A program with one keeps the
  full gate: unchanged tops cannot say it left a cell alone.
- A probe in a setup other than the judged one never takes that setup's
  acknowledgement.
- A program that cuts nothing was judged on the first setup's stock
  wherever it ran. carry::walk now takes its steps from the program's own
  ops when nothing is planned, so the program is judged on the setup it
  runs in, crossing setups by the same entry law as a cutting program.
  Cutting programs walk exactly as before.
- Across setups the walk cannot cross (a later setup's model stock, a
  machine change), such a program now refuses by name in the not-judged
  arm instead of posting: its ops' verdicts judge paths, not stock.

Also: the note says cell(s), and set_raw_stock_only's description and the
skill doc name report_inherited_deficits (reference regenerated).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
